 THE ARM FOR THE BRANCH THE MIGRATION ADDED. `web-send-http` used to hand back
 whatever the bare sender returned, so a response that stopped part way and one
 that went whole were the same value and the serve loop read the client's next
 request into the middle of a corrupted body. It now closes the connection when
 the send does not complete, and this is what shows that closing HAPPENS rather
 than being described.

 The fixtures are `net-send-capped`'s, which is deliberate: that arm proves the
 CHECKED SENDER reports incomplete, and this one proves the SERVER acts on the
 report. Two different claims, one fixture, and neither covers the other.

 `healthy` is the half that makes the other half mean something. A `web-send-http`
 that closed unconditionally would pass a truncation arm on its own.

 IT HAS TO BE PUT IN `TcpEstablished` BY HAND, and the first version of this arm
 did not: a session straight out of `net-session-new` is not connected, so the
 sender refuses it, the server closes, and BOTH rows read `yes` -- a control
 that agreed with its subject for the wrong reason. `net-send-capped` sets the
 state explicitly for the same arm and that is where this was taken from.

  cli-mac : List Integer = [82, 85, 10, 0, 2, 2]
  cli-ip : List Integer = [10, 0, 2, 100]
  srv-ip : List Integer = [10, 0, 2, 15]
  gw-ip : List Integer = [10, 0, 2, 2]

  seg0 : RexmitSeg = RexmitSeg { rx-frame = [], rx-ack = 0, rx-sent = 0, rx-resent = False }

  fill-queue : Integer, List RexmitSeg -> List RexmitSeg
  fill-queue (n) (acc) = if n <= 0 then acc else fill-queue (n - 1) (list-push acc seg0)

  base-sess : NetSession = net-session-new cli-mac cli-ip gw-ip 50000 80 srv-ip 1000

 The queue is full AND the connection is closed, exactly as `net-send-capped`
 sets it up: `net-io-send-drain` returns at its own closed check before it
 polls, so the arm needs no NIC.

  stalled : NetSession =
    let closed = set-conn base-sess (tcp-set-state (base-sess.conn) TcpClosed)
    in set-rexmit closed (fill-queue net-rexmit-capacity []) 3 0

  yn : Boolean -> Text
  yn (b) = if b then "yes" else "no"

Section: Entry

  opening : [Console, Network.Read, Network.Write] Nothing = act
    let resp = http-json "{\"ok\":true}"
    in let ts-stalled = transport-new stalled
    in let ts-healthy = transport-new (set-conn base-sess (tcp-set-state (base-sess.conn) TcpEstablished))
    in act
      short <- web-send-http ts-stalled resp
      print-line-uni ("stalled closed : " & yn (net-io-conn-closed short))
      whole <- web-send-http ts-healthy resp
      print-line-uni ("healthy closed : " & yn (net-io-conn-closed whole))
    end
  end
